  "rationale": "The representative comma context strongly overpredicts <END> even though the batch repeatedly continues with a person after an introductory comma. Reduce the generic end-after-punctuation rule while retaining explicit support for recognized sentence endings, exclamation marks, and the observed “for now.” closing. Add moderate, reusable support for person tokens after a comma, “for” after “all,” “was” after lowercase “that,” and “is” after “That” or “This.” These are local contextual tendencies, not claims that alternatives are impossible; commas and these words can occur in other constructions, and the replay gate must assess any regressions. The malformed free-generation sample is diagnostic only and is not treated as training evidence.",
